Uber | Phone Screen | L4 Design a Parking Lot
I got this question as phone screen, I was really not expecting it I thought this was meant to come in LLD interview and my role was for frontend.

Anyway the question was, implement a Parking Lot where you can park cars and bikes. Cars can only be assigned to car spots and bikes in both. The Parking Lot has multiple levels. You have to implement 3 functions: park(card_id), unpark(spot_id), check(card_id) -> spot_id

I found this question really hard, it may look simple but since it caught me by surprise I had to basically make decisions on how to structure things. What made me pause was "What is the strategy for parking a vehicle? How do I find a free spot?".I was not able to think on the very best solution in a minute so I started implementing what to me looked reasonable. I did a 3 dimensional matrix matrix[floor_index][vehicle_category][line_index]



My idea was, we keep score of how many vacant spots we have  on each floor, so we can find a floor to park in O(N). Something like this:

```
def findAvailableFloor(vehicle_category):
    for i in range(len(floorCounter[vehicle_category])):
        if floorCounter[i] > 0:
            return i
```


After finding a floor, we iterate over the spot array in the floor to find a free spot( a 0 in the array). That will give you a complexity of O(N+M).

```
